    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl">2. Not a gambling app</h2>
    <p>
      The App tosses a coin: it is a random-number tool and a decision aid. <strong
        >There is no stake, no wager and no prize</strong
      >, nothing can be won or lost in it, and no real or virtual money, chips or
      balance appear anywhere in it. The statistics screen counts throws, not
      winnings.
    </p>
    <p>
      Results are decided on your device by the platform's <strong
        >pseudo-random number generator</strong
      > — the same one behind the shuffle in any other app. Every result is
      decided before the coin starts moving: the spin is a picture of a toss that
      has already happened, not the thing that determines it. The coin is
      <em>fair</em> in the sense that heads and tails are equally likely. If you
      switch on <strong>landing on its edge</strong>, the coin will occasionally
      come to rest on its rim: that is not a result, it is not recorded in your
      statistics, and the coin is thrown again. We make no claim that results are
      random in a cryptographic sense, and the App must not be used where that is
      a requirement.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl">3. Ads and Pro</h2>
    <p>
      The free version shows banner ads provided by Google AdMob (see the
      <a href="/apps/coin-flip/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>); there are no
      full-screen and no rewarded ads. The one-time <strong>Pro</strong>
